      {
        "id": "p44-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find all the constant solutions of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=3x^2\\cos^2 y$ in the interval $-2\\pi\\le y\\le2\\pi$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2},\\ -\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},\\ \\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
          "worked": "For a constant solution, $y'=0$, so $\\cos^2 y=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\cos y&=0\\\\\ny&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+k\\pi,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIn $-2\\pi\\le y\\le2\\pi$, the constant solutions are $$y=-\\frac{3\\pi}{2},\\ -\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\ \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q20-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find all the non-constant solutions.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\tan^{-1}(x^3+C)+k\\pi$, where $C\\in\\mathbb R$ and $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.",
          "worked": "For $\\cos y\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 y}\\,dy&=3x^2\\,dx\\\\\n\\sec^2 y\\,dy&=3x^2\\,dx\\\\\n\\int\\sec^2 y\\,dy&=\\int3x^2\\,dx\\\\\n\\tan y&=x^3+C\\\\\ny&=\\tan^{-1}(x^3+C)+k\\pi,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\n\\end{align*}$$\nHere $C$ is any real constant; $k\\pi$ includes every branch of the inverse tangent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 39
      }
    ]
  },
